   "type": 0,
   "text": "1\nI don't think they have many problems going to Paraguay\nMost people will probably buy them (if they aren't crazy expensive) just to show off and feel American \n\nMaybe the biggest problems are on the legal side and politics\nBecause there is a lot of corruption in Paraguay\nhttps://www.economist.com/the-americas/2023/02/02/the-united-states-says-corruption-in-paraguay-starts-at-the-top\n\n2) internet and electricity are not stable, depending on the location power failures are  something that happens multiple times per month\nSo investing in an auxiliary power system is a good idea",
